All checks confirm:
- Router4 is UP: eth0 (.200.1 LAN), eth4 (to router5), eth5 (to router3) all UP; RIP stable with two neighbours
- PC11 can ping its gateway (192.168.200.1) and all Location C peers (PC12–PC14)
- PC11 reaches Location A (PC4 at 172.16.10.4) with 0% loss via router4 → router5 → router0
- The only unreachable segment is Location B (172.18.50/51.x). Traceroute confirms packets traverse router4→router3→router6 successfully, then are dropped at router6 by an iptables FORWARD ACL blocking all TCP/UDP/ICMP arriving on eth2 (the backbone-facing interface). This is the documented baseline security policy on router6, not an injected fault.

